    "field": "Ice sheet dynamics",
    "problem": "This paper addresses the challenge of understanding the potential collapse of the West Antarctic Ice Sheet, proposing that the unbuttressed Thwaites and Pine Island Glaciers flowing into Pine Island Bay create a \"weak underbelly\" that could initiate a rapid, widespread disintegration of the marine ice sheet.",
    "method": "This paper proposes a numerical model to simulate marine ice-sheet collapse by coupling equations for grounding-line retreat, ice-stream downdraw, and isostatic rebound, thereby integrating the key ice-ocean, ice-atmosphere, and ice-bed interactions that drive the system.",
    "task": "The task is to formulate and numerically test a scenario for the disintegration of the West Antarctic ice sheet, proposing that its collapse is initiated by surges of glaciers into Pine Island Bay.",
    "model": [
        "CLIMAP"
    ],
